WEBVTT

00:00.390 --> 00:10.530
Tsuki no kaasu tsumetai yume no naka de

00:00.390 --> 00:10.530
Under the moon’s curse, inside of a cold dream…

00:19.040 --> 00:25.420
Kotoba no nai sekai de bokura wa ai wo kataru

00:19.040 --> 00:25.420
In a world without words, we speak of love

00:25.420 --> 00:29.380
itsuka kimi ni todoku made

00:25.420 --> 00:29.380
until it reaches you someday.

00:32.220 --> 00:39.100
Kizu darake no kaina de dakiyoseta kuchibiru no

00:32.220 --> 00:39.100
I want to melt the frozen over wish...

00:39.100 --> 00:44.770
haritsumeta negai tokashitakute

00:39.100 --> 00:44.770
from the lips that I embraced with arms covered in wounds.

00:45.020 --> 00:51.730
Nee, aishiatta kako no utsukushisa sutesareba

00:45.020 --> 00:51.730
Hey, if I abandon the beauty of the past when we loved each other,

00:52.110 --> 00:57.910
ashita motto kirei na yoru e yukeru kara

00:52.110 --> 00:57.910
then tomorrow, I can go to a more beautiful night.

00:58.280 --> 01:06.460
Tsuki no kaasu tsumetai yume no naka kara

00:58.280 --> 01:06.460
Under the moon’s curse, from inside of a cold dream.

01:06.460 --> 01:13.130
Kimi wo tooku tsuresaritakute

01:06.460 --> 01:13.130
I want to take you somewhere far away,

01:13.130 --> 01:16.550
doko made yukeru

01:13.130 --> 01:16.550
and go anywhere,

01:16.550 --> 01:24.140
ai wo shinjite ii basho made

01:16.550 --> 01:24.140
to a place where we can believe in love.

01:38.010 --> 01:38.910
Welcome.

01:39.780 --> 01:40.530
Right on time.

01:53.200 --> 01:55.910
So, what are you here for today, Kaidou?

01:57.530 --> 02:02.470
I want to consult with
you, but not about me.

02:02.600 --> 02:07.940
The scenario of a male
student at an art university (Age 20)

02:03.130 --> 02:07.400
Case 1: The scenario of a male
student at an art university (Age 20)

02:08.560 --> 02:11.400
My friend has been acting strange lately.

02:13.200 --> 02:13.860
Hello.

02:15.420 --> 02:16.610
How does it look?

02:17.450 --> 02:19.030
The target has moved.

02:19.620 --> 02:21.350
Don't lose sight of it.

02:21.350 --> 02:22.400
Roger.

02:22.400 --> 02:23.700
Pursuit will begin.

02:29.890 --> 02:31.000
Target confirmed!

02:32.780 --> 02:33.460
In front of the station!

02:34.160 --> 02:36.010
Just now, he is being
contacted by his comrades.

02:38.290 --> 02:41.250
Some girl she is...

02:41.250 --> 02:43.640
She shows her bellybutton
even though it's not summer.

02:44.550 --> 02:48.040
Soubi, you better be careful
or Ritsuka's going to be taken.

02:48.040 --> 02:49.890
Don't worry about that.

02:49.890 --> 02:50.730
Don't lose them.

02:51.120 --> 02:55.200
Sunday, his behavior was
peculiar, so I followed him.

02:56.640 --> 02:58.910
He's, in one word, a pervert...

02:58.910 --> 03:01.030
I mean, a stalker!

03:01.800 --> 03:08.410
So, Kaidou... Now you're
stalking that friend in turn.

03:08.660 --> 03:09.620
No!

03:11.320 --> 03:12.080
Anyway!

03:12.690 --> 03:14.890
The grade-schoolers transferred at
Jiyuugaoka to a...

03:14.890 --> 03:17.070
...Motomachi Chinatown bound train...

03:19.390 --> 03:21.770
...and arrived at Yokohama Minato Mirai.

03:22.850 --> 03:24.860
Wow, we're here!

03:26.730 --> 03:28.120
Of course, we did too.

03:32.530 --> 03:33.170
Huh?

03:33.990 --> 03:35.230
Who are you looking for?

03:36.320 --> 03:38.460
Oh, Soubi!

03:38.460 --> 03:40.110
What are you doing here?

03:40.350 --> 03:43.320
What a coincidence. I mean, really!

03:50.380 --> 03:51.720
Thank you, my friend...

03:52.340 --> 03:56.530
I might lose him by myself, but
with two people, it'll be easy.

03:58.090 --> 04:01.960
I'm letting you know now that
I won't help you commit a crime!

04:02.470 --> 04:03.450
Don't worry.

04:05.170 --> 04:06.470
This is a formality of love.

04:19.260 --> 04:21.220
Didn't she notice you?

04:21.610 --> 04:22.320
Who knows?

04:23.580 --> 04:27.280
I see. So that lady
is the school teacher.

04:28.210 --> 04:31.780
But why is she with
those brats on a Sunday?

04:31.780 --> 04:32.660
Don't know.

04:33.210 --> 04:36.530
You really have no
interests other than Ritsuka.

04:38.790 --> 04:40.920
He's checking his cellphone again.

04:42.720 --> 04:45.380
I'm sorry to say I won't
be text messaging you today.

04:46.490 --> 04:49.750
...Ritsuka, you're only a kid... I
guess you don't know yet.

04:50.060 --> 04:52.230
When you are not together...

04:51.770 --> 04:53.940
...you think about him more.

04:59.520 --> 05:01.630
What are you thinking about?

05:01.630 --> 05:03.190
Creepy!

05:03.800 --> 05:05.230
Hurry, hurry!

05:08.520 --> 05:09.990
So, so, what should we ride?

05:10.380 --> 05:12.640
I'm fine with whatever Yuiko likes.

05:14.020 --> 05:16.080
Ritsuka, what do you like?

05:16.080 --> 05:20.610
Hey, rather than doing this, why
don't you just go play with him?

05:25.350 --> 05:26.220
I can't...

05:26.410 --> 05:27.010
What?

05:27.960 --> 05:31.800
Last night, he told me not to come here.

05:32.200 --> 05:35.010
You look delighted about that.

05:35.480 --> 05:36.640
I'm waiting.

05:37.360 --> 05:38.660
I'll go later...

05:38.660 --> 05:39.360
Huh?

05:40.360 --> 05:44.160
After he thoroughly
experiences some time without me.

05:45.750 --> 05:48.530
Whoa, what a nasty plan!

05:52.300 --> 05:54.780
It looks like they're
going to ride that one.

05:59.030 --> 06:00.040
H-Hey!

06:00.410 --> 06:02.420
Where are you going?

06:04.550 --> 06:06.510
Wait, hey!

06:11.140 --> 06:12.070
Hey...

06:14.950 --> 06:17.020
What's going on all of a sudden?

06:18.020 --> 06:19.090
You can't see.

06:19.090 --> 06:19.560
Huh?

06:20.470 --> 06:22.520
You can't see inside the
ride from there.

06:25.640 --> 06:26.440
Fool...

06:32.300 --> 06:33.510
I can tell, Ritsuka.

06:34.420 --> 06:38.180
You're wishing Soubi was there with you...

06:38.700 --> 06:40.710
Maybe he feels liberated...

06:41.460 --> 06:43.670
...not having a pervert around him.

06:43.670 --> 06:46.050
Kio, I'm not a pervert...

06:47.760 --> 06:49.720
Ritsuka Aoyagi is hugging a girl!

06:51.800 --> 06:53.010
That's nonsense.

06:53.380 --> 06:55.150
I don't know...

06:55.150 --> 06:58.700
Grade-schoolers are
pretty forward these days...

06:58.700 --> 06:59.020
Give me.

07:13.570 --> 07:15.610
See? Didn't I tell ya?

07:16.130 --> 07:18.070
They probably kissed.

07:18.420 --> 07:20.380
Maybe more.

07:20.990 --> 07:21.620
Yo?

07:22.400 --> 07:24.220
Soubi!

07:24.220 --> 07:27.090
Give up on Ritsuka already!

07:37.790 --> 07:38.500
Let's go!

07:38.770 --> 07:39.620
Where?

07:39.620 --> 07:40.470
Ferris wheel.

07:41.400 --> 07:43.110
I just got off that!

07:43.110 --> 07:44.000
Come on!

07:44.560 --> 07:48.320
Besides, why are you here?
I told you not to come!

07:48.980 --> 07:51.540
Why do you always break your promises?

07:51.540 --> 07:52.280
Hey!

07:53.410 --> 07:54.130
Go home!

07:55.040 --> 07:56.510
Go right now!

07:56.510 --> 07:57.620
Leave!

07:58.440 --> 07:59.830
Go already!

08:07.840 --> 08:13.320
After that, we boarded the water bus
and headed towards Yamashita Park.

08:17.110 --> 08:20.060
But oddly enough, by the time we got off...

08:22.940 --> 08:27.600
...both he and Ritsuka Aoyagi were back to
normal.

08:28.910 --> 08:31.940
Why do you think so?

08:33.470 --> 08:34.490
Ritsuka...

08:35.150 --> 08:38.330
Ritsuka, on the Ferris
wheel with a girl...

08:40.170 --> 08:42.910
Um, Doc?

08:45.140 --> 08:46.470
Doc?

09:06.060 --> 09:10.940
The scenario of a female
grade-school teacher. (Age 23)

09:06.650 --> 09:10.430
Case Two: The scenario of a female
grade-school teacher.

09:11.820 --> 09:14.740
It was Saturday, after school.

09:15.420 --> 09:16.410
Yokohama?

09:16.570 --> 09:18.320
Come on, let's go!

09:18.960 --> 09:22.750
The weather tomorrow's supposed to
be great, so let's go to Yokohama!

09:23.160 --> 09:26.120
But there's a book I wanted to read...

09:26.300 --> 09:28.190
Come on, Aoyagi.

09:28.880 --> 09:31.020
The international city of Yokohama.

09:31.020 --> 09:33.780
The lovers' port town of Yokohama.

09:33.780 --> 09:37.550
You'll definitely make great memories.

09:38.600 --> 09:39.430
Memories...

09:40.380 --> 09:41.880
You're going too, Yayoi?

09:41.880 --> 09:42.750
Of course!

09:42.750 --> 09:43.310
Huh?

09:43.580 --> 09:46.190
I see, then, maybe I'll go...

09:47.010 --> 09:48.050
Oh, really?

09:48.050 --> 09:48.750
Yeah...

09:49.210 --> 09:50.390
Then it's a plan.

09:50.730 --> 09:52.730
I'm not sure about that idea.

09:53.480 --> 09:56.200
What are you kids
going to do in Yokohama?

09:56.200 --> 10:01.180
Well, we'll look at the boats, go
shopping, and eat yummy foods...

10:01.180 --> 10:03.160
You can't do those in Sangenjaya?

10:03.160 --> 10:05.380
You can't see the ocean in Sangenjaya!

10:05.380 --> 10:06.510
I know!

10:07.140 --> 10:09.030
Teacher, would you like to come with us?

10:10.120 --> 10:10.880
But...

10:11.210 --> 10:16.090
Don't ask her that! I'm sure
she has dates on Sundays.

10:16.980 --> 10:18.350
Right, Teacher?

10:20.090 --> 10:25.810
And so on Sunday, I ended
up chaperoning my students.

10:26.200 --> 10:28.270
So, you guys, where do you want to go?

10:28.610 --> 10:32.230
Let's see, the Yokohama Foreigner's
Cemetery is a good date spot.

10:32.360 --> 10:33.820
A cemetery?

10:33.820 --> 10:35.600
Yayoi, that's weird!

10:35.600 --> 10:38.510
Oh, Ritsuka, what are
you doing, text messaging?

10:38.510 --> 10:39.380
N-No...

10:40.680 --> 10:42.340
Stop it!

10:42.340 --> 10:43.670
Come on, why not?

10:54.550 --> 10:55.590
Agatsuma!

11:02.680 --> 11:04.410
What am I thinking?

11:04.410 --> 11:06.770
There's no way Agatsuma's here.

11:18.440 --> 11:20.570
What's got into me?

11:20.570 --> 11:23.410
I'm hallucinating about Agatsuma...

11:26.500 --> 11:28.450
No! Just my imagination!

11:28.450 --> 11:30.080
Right, my imagination.

11:44.900 --> 11:48.350
What am I going to do?
Hallucinating in broad daylight!

11:51.680 --> 11:53.310
Yuiko!

11:54.570 --> 11:56.110
Yuiko...

11:58.450 --> 12:01.990
There's no point in riding the
Ferris wheel with my students...

12:02.490 --> 12:03.070
If anything...

12:10.420 --> 12:11.590
A-Agatsuma!

12:13.050 --> 12:14.550
Stupid, stupid, stupid, stupid, stupid...

12:14.550 --> 12:16.390
I have to get a grip!

12:16.390 --> 12:19.590
Stupid Hitomi! Stupid,
stupid, stupid, stupid...

12:20.850 --> 12:21.520
What's wrong?

12:22.890 --> 12:25.600
Yuiko and Aoyagi are...

12:30.480 --> 12:31.350
Don't tell me...

12:32.370 --> 12:33.670
These ears...

12:33.670 --> 12:34.520
Let's get rid of them.

12:35.030 --> 12:36.320
No way!

12:36.320 --> 12:38.980
I haven't even done it...

12:39.610 --> 12:41.490
But it's not ridiculous.

12:41.490 --> 12:45.570
Grade-schoolers these
days are unusually forward.

12:46.000 --> 12:48.680
Yuiko! Yuiko!

12:48.680 --> 12:49.580
Yuiko!

12:50.580 --> 12:54.540
Already being 23, maybe it's
strange not having anything happen...

12:55.710 --> 12:58.500
Maybe that's why I'm hallucinating.

13:03.430 --> 13:04.760
We're finally here!

13:06.060 --> 13:07.560
That was fun.

13:07.560 --> 13:09.690
You were scared...

13:09.690 --> 13:10.510
Ritsuka!

13:14.060 --> 13:14.980
Let's go!

13:14.980 --> 13:15.930
Where?

13:15.930 --> 13:16.830
Ferris wheel.

13:18.190 --> 13:20.400
Is he really here?

13:22.700 --> 13:27.540
After all that, I wasn't hallucinating.
He was really there.

13:29.290 --> 13:33.580
But for him, I might
as well not have been there.

13:35.550 --> 13:39.380
But by the time we went to
Yamashita Park by water bus...

13:40.700 --> 13:43.710
...his attitude had completely changed...

13:43.710 --> 13:48.760
...of course towards Aoyagi, but
he was also nice to everybody...

13:50.330 --> 13:52.540
...and at Chinatown...

13:53.100 --> 13:54.220
Here, Teacher...

13:56.020 --> 13:58.230
He was also...

14:02.550 --> 14:05.430
I'm fine with just that...

14:05.430 --> 14:09.800
He looked at me! He didn't ignore me!

14:10.210 --> 14:12.120
Just for that, I'm...

14:13.920 --> 14:17.040
Bartender, another one for her.

14:17.040 --> 14:18.390
Certainly.

14:22.720 --> 14:25.460
Melon and watermelon juice.

14:26.190 --> 14:27.250
Juice?

14:27.250 --> 14:29.840
Yes, non-alcoholic.

14:38.020 --> 14:42.980
The scenario of
an elementary-school boy. (Age 12)

14:38.980 --> 14:42.250
Case Three: The Scenario of
an elementary-school boy.

14:44.200 --> 14:45.480
Memory making?

14:47.330 --> 14:47.820
Okay.

14:48.590 --> 14:50.240
You have nothing to do with this, Soubi!

14:51.200 --> 14:52.120
Is that so?

14:52.120 --> 14:52.990
That is so!

14:53.830 --> 14:57.450
Your photos keep adding up.
This isn't much of a collection!

14:58.150 --> 15:01.960
Tomorrow, I'm gonna make memories with
my school friends and take lots of photos!

15:02.130 --> 15:03.790
You don't need to come!

15:07.390 --> 15:09.290
W-What?

15:10.440 --> 15:11.260
Nothing...

15:12.300 --> 15:14.710
Fine. You don't need to take me.

15:15.110 --> 15:17.020
If you're fine, then
don't say it like that.

15:19.860 --> 15:20.270
Ritsuka.

15:23.600 --> 15:24.060
Good night.

15:33.080 --> 15:34.230
That guy...

15:35.120 --> 15:39.150
I thought he'd interfere by
texting me weird messages.

15:39.150 --> 15:39.910
Hey? Hey?

15:41.040 --> 15:42.920
What do you want, Ritsuka?

15:43.550 --> 15:45.750
I know, the Ferris wheel, right?

15:45.750 --> 15:46.210
Hey!

15:46.510 --> 15:48.700
Miss Shinonome, go with Yayoi, okay?

15:50.400 --> 15:51.830
Shall we...

15:52.180 --> 15:53.070
Okay...

15:53.770 --> 15:56.860
It's gonna fall!

15:57.490 --> 15:59.860
If you're afraid of heights, why...

15:59.860 --> 16:03.230
Because I wanted to
ride it alone with you!

16:03.650 --> 16:04.560
That's why...

16:06.980 --> 16:09.610
I don't wanna anymore! Let me off!

16:09.610 --> 16:12.530
It's high! I'm scared!

16:12.840 --> 16:15.910
It's pretty windy up here...

16:22.580 --> 16:23.830
So beautiful...

16:27.630 --> 16:30.400
I want to show this to him...

16:35.710 --> 16:36.630
Ow...

16:38.730 --> 16:41.100
Oh, so that's what it was!

16:42.110 --> 16:43.480
What do you mean?

16:43.760 --> 16:46.310
N-No, nothing...

16:46.310 --> 16:47.440
Nothing at all.

16:47.790 --> 16:48.910
I see, then?

16:48.910 --> 16:49.730
And then...?

16:52.620 --> 16:53.360
Yeah.

16:55.150 --> 16:58.400
When we got off, he was there.

17:00.490 --> 17:01.120
Ritsuka.

17:01.780 --> 17:02.870
Go home!

17:03.290 --> 17:04.530
Go right now!

17:04.910 --> 17:06.350
Leave!

17:16.310 --> 17:18.990
You're Seimei's younger brother.

17:22.500 --> 17:25.550
You know about Seimei?

17:25.550 --> 17:26.590
Nah.

17:28.720 --> 17:32.760
I know the guy who was
owned by Seimei Aoyagi.

17:34.570 --> 17:36.280
Wow! That's the Rainbow Bridge!

17:36.690 --> 17:38.260
That's in Odaiba.

17:38.740 --> 17:40.200
That's the Bay Bridge.

17:41.210 --> 17:43.290
Ohhh, Soubi, you're so knowledgeable.

17:43.670 --> 17:47.250
He was always torn up because of Seimei...

17:48.410 --> 17:53.470
...but the worst part was that
he was content with that...

17:56.010 --> 17:57.770
I hate to say this to you...

17:57.770 --> 18:01.720
...but when I heard that Seimei
had died, honestly, I was relieved.

18:02.750 --> 18:06.730
I thought he'd finally be released...

18:07.940 --> 18:09.020
...but I was wrong.

18:10.440 --> 18:13.840
He became like a zombie...

18:15.150 --> 18:19.520
Seimei died, but he
still controlled Soubi.

18:21.960 --> 18:24.160
But It's okay now.

18:25.480 --> 18:29.910
As Seimei's brother, I was
imagining the worst brat...

18:30.470 --> 18:32.160
...but you're pretty normal.

18:32.160 --> 18:33.880
Sorry for being normal.

18:33.880 --> 18:35.200
Don't be sorry...

18:35.880 --> 18:37.970
...although I don't want to admit it.

18:39.700 --> 18:42.470
He returned, thanks to you...

18:43.420 --> 18:45.180
...from zombie to human.

18:50.100 --> 18:51.220
Yeah!

18:53.280 --> 18:54.900
Hawatari, be careful!

18:55.240 --> 18:56.190
Okay?

18:57.870 --> 18:59.940
You tried to catch a butterfly?

19:01.250 --> 19:04.170
Yuiko told me...

19:04.700 --> 19:07.260
...that there was a
butterfly in the Ferris wheel.

19:08.090 --> 19:09.080
Yeah.

19:09.080 --> 19:10.880
So, did you catch it?

19:11.420 --> 19:14.090
No, I tried...

19:15.220 --> 19:17.050
...but it disappeared somewhere.

19:17.800 --> 19:20.230
Is it true that you think of
me when you see a butterfly?

19:21.170 --> 19:21.700
What?

19:23.790 --> 19:25.810
Yuiko told you that, too?

19:26.350 --> 19:26.970
Ritsuka.

19:36.990 --> 19:37.820
Caught ya.

20:09.860 --> 20:15.770
I didn't know it was so much
fun to play with everybody.

20:27.080 --> 20:32.330
I didn't know what to do when I
was told that somebody liked me.

20:33.860 --> 20:37.040
But now, everybody...

20:43.470 --> 20:49.230
I like Yuiko, I like Yayoi,
I like Miss Shinonome...

20:50.320 --> 20:52.930
...I like Soubi's friend called Kio...

20:53.900 --> 20:56.220
...and of course, Soubi, <i>too...</i>

20:58.280 --> 21:00.500
...I see, that's great.

21:01.110 --> 21:03.200
So did you take a lot of pictures?

21:03.490 --> 21:04.060
Huh?

21:05.160 --> 21:08.290
No, I took almost none.

21:08.290 --> 21:09.910
Oh, why?

21:11.000 --> 21:13.370
Yeah, well...

21:14.210 --> 21:18.380
...I was having so much fun with
everybody, I forgot.

21:29.720 --> 21:34.640
To be continued...

21:31.010 --> 21:40.570
Setsunasa no kagiri made dakishimete mo

21:31.010 --> 21:40.570
Even if I hold you with all my suffering,

21:41.440 --> 21:50.950
itsu made mo hitotsu ni wa narenakute

21:41.440 --> 21:50.950
we still can't be one.

21:51.540 --> 22:01.460
Yasashisa yori fukai basho de fureau no wa itami dake

21:51.540 --> 22:01.460
The only thing that we can feel deep within besides kindness is pain,

22:01.880 --> 22:09.470
futari wo musunde kudasai

22:01.880 --> 22:09.470
so please, bind the two of us together.

22:12.010 --> 22:16.850
Bokura wa mou yume wo minai

22:12.010 --> 22:16.850
We no longer dream anymore,

22:16.850 --> 22:21.980
tomadoinagara te wo totte

22:16.850 --> 22:21.980
when you're wavering, take my hand

22:22.270 --> 22:31.200
zankoku na yoake no hou e arukidasu

22:22.270 --> 22:31.200
as we tread towards the cruel light of dawn.

22:32.330 --> 22:42.340
Hontou no kotoba wa kitto hontou no sekai no dokoka

22:32.330 --> 22:42.340
I'm sure real words are somewhere in the real world.

22:42.670 --> 22:51.550
Bokura no mukuchi na yoru ni hisonderu

22:42.670 --> 22:51.550
They lurk in the shadows of our silent nights.

22:51.930 --> 22:57.060
Ima mo kitto

22:51.930 --> 22:57.060
Surely, even now...

23:00.440 --> 23:06.650
One day, suddenly, when you least
expect it. Fate changes dramatically.

23:06.650 --> 23:09.580
